ype/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273076} {:answer/id #uuid "542425f7-6cb3-5652-b4c4-c4e7fd2c0916" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273105} {:answer/id #uuid "5d4f8557-52a4-5276-a1e1-4b5aaf1bd9f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273190} {:answer/id #uuid "8eb6ea03-73f9-5ab9-bec2-771fcf49b774" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273623} {:answer/id #uuid "bc2a5003-9e7c-551d-aa36-6e3b23569a84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274015}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc2a5003-9e7c-551d-aa36-6e3b23569a84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274015} :answer-field/id #uuid "c987bfcc-3ddd-51b1-9ee6-0c54d27baf82" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274987}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e87161c3-2cae-55f5-bb92-55f97a5739b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-158026" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}{x}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275419 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28ef5c14-78d0-5208-855a-6b41a420438a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272752} {:answer/id #uuid "80fed0a8-073f-57d9-9a9b-52a42a33835b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\text{ }\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273493} {:answer/id #uuid "82123406-b934-5a9c-8160-0677d7d54cac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273499} {:answer/id #uuid "c3e404da-fc1a-5a36-9bce-6763d8f34e26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274086} {:answer/id #uuid "d122fedc-b019-5f58-8be1-37fe87dddc8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274209}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d122fedc-b019-5f58-8be1-37fe87dddc8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274209} :answer-field/id #uuid "e400646f-8ad1-5f1d-ad65-32dd857ca29e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275035}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c0d607e3-0c1a-5227-a757-1fdd9227cb73" :question/math-academy-id "q-158027" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot {y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275421 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01b03335-77aa-59fa-b7e8-6e2269d546b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272397} {:answer/id #uuid "719ee0ff-8189-52e3-bc17-a3256803c517" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273361} {:answer/id #uuid "7f2e38d7-f3bf-597e-9a67-9bf1f67d04c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273480} {:answer/id #uuid "a4697080-8561-5e7e-b488-d65e1a6352a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273806} {:answer/id #uuid "abf0e68e-bca8-580f-9a48-d359bd48f72f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273870}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01b03335-77aa-59fa-b7e8-6e2269d546b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272397} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ffe6dcc-9fa6-5228-9a8e-a4756f2ab21b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274769}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7037401f-27c0-588d-a952-7eb3ef7b14ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-158030" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{y}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x\\cdot \\frac{1}{y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\ny\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275422 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71673ba5-a378-5710-9335-cc0008aef108" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3x}{5x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273358} {:answer/id #uuid "7d32ab15-cbb6-55a1-b112-149aeef16cab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5x+1}{3x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273458} {:answer/id #uuid "893d3a4c-5ba0-5b1b-a19f-e339fc0dc9cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5xy+y}{3x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273570} {:answer/id #uuid "c621efd1-dd66-5976-9fe1-f299c7ad75bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x+1}{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274106} {:answer/id #uuid "f01057d5-b998-5b8f-8b95-f2363bc35510" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3x}{5x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f01057d5-b998-5b8f-8b95-f2363bc35510" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3x}{5x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274513} :answer-field/id #uuid "e450d81c-8d75-511b-8599-f5fc6a521993" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275036}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fe104c00-01e9-59b5-87fa-d82fed8f3827" :question/math-academy-id "q-158032" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3x}{5xy+y}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3x}{(5x+1)y} \\\\  & =\\frac{3x}{5x+1}\\cdot \\frac{1}{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\ny\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3x}{5x+1}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Separating the Variables in a Differential Equation"}]}
